{"question_id": "466", "answer": "\\(\\operatorname{Spec}_S(\\operatorname{Sym}_{\\mathcal O_S}(E))\\)", "grade": "INCORRECT", "call": {"instrument": "grader", "model": "gemini-3.8-flash", "question_id": "466", "tier": 4, "input_tokens": 1552, "output_tokens": 270, "usd": "0.0021765", "latency_s": 5.6979009360075, "reply": "B", "served_model": "gemini-3.8-flash", "reasoning_tokens": 269, "effort": "", "truncated": false}}
{"question_id": "466", "answer": "**The symmetric algebra $\\mathrm{Sym}_{\\mathcal O_S}(\\mathcal E)=\\bigoplus_{n\\ge 0}\\mathrm{Sym}^n(\\mathcal E)$**, which is quasi-coherent and graded. So $\\mathbb V(\\mathcal E)=\\underline{\\mathrm{Spec}}_S\\big(\\mathrm{Sym}_{\\mathcal O_S}(\\mathcal E)\\big)$.\n\nWith this undualized convention, a $T$-point of $\\mathbb V(\\mathcal E)$ over $S$ is an $\\mathcal O_T$-linear map $\\mathcal E_T\\to\\mathcal O_T$. Hence the sheaf of sections of $\\mathbb V(\\mathcal E)$ is the dual $\\mathcal E^\\vee$, not $\\mathcal E$ itself.", "grade": "CORRECT", "call": {"instrument": "grader", "model": "gemini-3.8-flash", "question_id": "466", "tier": 4, "input_tokens": 1684, "output_tokens": 172, "usd": "0.001908", "latency_s": 3.730042670998955, "reply": "A", "served_model": "gemini-3.8-flash", "reasoning_tokens": 171, "effort": "", "truncated": false}}
