{"question_id": "479", "answer": "$$\\bar\\theta_U=\\frac{2\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i}{\\chi^2_{2n,\\,1-\\alpha}}=\\frac{2n\\bar X}{\\chi^2_{2n,\\,1-\\alpha}}$$\n\nHere $\\chi^2_{2n,1-\\alpha}$ is the upper $1-\\alpha$ point, i.e. the lower $\\alpha$ quantile, of $\\chi^2_{2n}$. This follows because $2\\sum X_i/\\theta \\sim \\chi^2_{2n}$.\n\nThe UMA $1-\\alpha$ confidence set is therefore $0<\\theta\\le \\dfrac{2\\sum X_i}{\\chi^2_{2n,1-\\alpha}}$.", "grade": "INCORRECT", "call": {"instrument": "grader", "model": "gemini-3.8-flash", "question_id": "479", "tier": 4, "input_tokens": 1713, "output_tokens": 678, "usd": "0.00382725", "latency_s": 5.04891570500331, "reply": "B", "served_model": "gemini-3.8-flash", "reasoning_tokens": 677, "effort": "", "truncated": false}}
